<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harem conspiracy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1153 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a> · Also known as harem conspirators</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Harem conspiracy was a plot within the royal household against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">Pharaoh</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-iii">Ramesses III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> around 1153 BCE. Records of the trial of the conspirators survive, and forensic study of his mummy indicates that he was killed. His death was followed by a series of weaker rulers, part of the decline of the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harem-conspiracy.jpg" alt="Harem conspiracy" width="320" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Weihrauchopfer_RamsesIII_aus_KV11.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
